<li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-connection.html">Connections and authentication</a>: ordinary and reserved admission and the resource cost of the connection ceiling.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/diskusage.html">Monitoring disk usage</a>: object space and full-volume failure. <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/sql-vacuum.html">VACUUM</a>: reuse, rewriting, locks and space requirements.</li>
<li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/runtime-config-client.html">Client connection defaults</a>: statement, lock, idle-transaction and transaction timeouts. <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/functions-admin.html#FUNCTIONS-ADMIN-SIGNAL">Server signalling functions</a>: cancellation, termination, bounded waiting and authority.</li>
<li><a href="https://node-postgres.com/apis/pool">node-postgres Pool</a>: borrowed and queued clients, release and pool counters. <a href="https://node-postgres.com/features/transactions">Transactions</a>: keeping transaction work on one client.</li>
